Not really notable, since it's a Valkyre ascension, which tbh I now
consider easy given how easy the planes were and how unnecessary my
second /oW really was. But, if you want to come up with notable things
about it:

1) It was the very first character I ever created on a public server
(alt.org)
2) I didn't get crazy help from a bones file (I did get a little, but
not like a full AK or even a BoH, just a [oMR and some rings)
3) I actually had two of the easier conducts (polyselfless & no wish
for artifacts)

Quick run down of the major events:

Spent some time playing with the graphics settings, cygwin's terminal
sucks so I downloaded PuTTY which was much better for nethackage.

Dlvl 1 only seemed to have two rooms, second room did have the
downstair.... eventually found the secret door in the room I checked
second.

Grabbed an orcish dagger to force a lock, it welded to my hand! Crap,
YASD incoming. Found an altar on dlvl 2, found a bunch of food on dlvl
3 so I figured I'd play with the altar for awhile. I tried to lure
baddies into the room only to have them jump into the teleport trap
right next to the altar. Tried to set up a stash of random equipment
there, but the trap just made it too annoying. Managed to get Mjollnir
out of it but then the same homonuculous jumped in the trap three
times so I gave up. Also didn't manage to get enough monsters to get
my luck high enough to try to pray the curse off, so I resorted to
dipping it in fountains. Dried up 3 fountains trying to get my now
thoroughly rusty corroded -1 cursed orcish dagger out of my hand... I
#named it "pudding farm!". In the process my dog got killed by a
Gnomish Wizard on Dlvl3 when I was only XP 5.

Things went on pretty uneventfully, I found a cat who I named Idefix
and then Minetown turned out to be a bones level for a low level
wizard who died IN Izchak's. So I had to buy everything out of the
shop because it was all cursed. I had a blessed ?o80gp, so I put his
[oMR on and read it carrying all the rest of his stuff hoping it was
Remove Curse, and it was. Woot. So now I had a MM and a [oMR and two
300 gp rings, one of which was conflict and the other wasn't
polymorph. Unfortunately as usual the rng had me short on ?oID though
unlike my last post on here the ?oID I did get later actually hit the
ID-all twice in a row. Also I got a BoH from the hardware store, which
was pretty sweet. Also managed to put together enough cash for 1 round
of protection from the altar.

I ran through the mines, got the luckstone, maxed my luck a different
altar in the main dungeon with a bag of tricks and a /oCM I found,
went to put the bag of tricks in my chest when.... whoops... i typed
"ao" instead of "l", didn't I... "You have been hit by a magical
explosion!" nooooooooooooo there go all my scrolls and potions not to
mention the BoH. Sigh. At least I'm not dead. Went and did sokoban now
praying for BoH but Odin decided to answer my earlier prayers and gave
me the "oR.

So I proceeded down the dungeon in my meticulously researched random
drop blessed dwarf gear (mithril coat, iron shoes, iron helm) plus my
starting shield, the ]oMR and the "oR. XP 11, found my quest, found
ludios on the next level down. I figured what the hell, my AC isn't
awful and I have Mjollnir and conflict. Maybe I'll get Dragon Scales
without a wish???

Long story short, a /oPoly droppped in the treasure zoo, but before I
started on that business there was a gray dragon flying around.
Unfortunately I dropped him to 3 hp and he got scared and wouldn't
stop flying over the moat for me to kill him no matter how hard I
tried to herd him to the wall. Eventually I had to LEAVE ludios, come
back later when he had regenned to full hp, and killed him... no
scales. Sigh.

I had no way to get over the moat other than a scroll of earth, so I
did that and then let the throne room kill Croesus (I wasn't sure my
AC & HP could handle him in melee). A ring of searching made quick
work of the the vault and I went to skin AC 1.

Spent a long time moving all the soldier gear into 4 piles praying for
magic stuff and managed to get:
Every single type of magic boot EXCEPT speed
A cursed -1 Helm of Telepathy
+0 Gauntlets of... Dexterity
+0 Hawaiian Shirt (hadn't seen one yet)
+0 Silver saber (hadn't seen one yet)

I was short on ID though, I just knew none of the magic boots were
cursed and none of them made me get faster. One did make me levitate
though, so I used that to kill Medusa and proceed down to the castle.
But in the meantime I got careless around a pyrolisk and lost all my
potions and scrolls AGAIN. I was starved for both as a result the
whole game. I hear people talking about how their stash has 40 holy
waters and 100 scrolls before the ascension run, lol, I think I had
like 10 potions total and maybe 15 scrolls before I woke Rodney.

This was my first time making this far not in explore mode, I had
never actually faced liches and master mind flayers in a real game
before. Did NOT want to get my brain sucked and I had no scrolls of
genocide left... but of course the last monsters standing after
conflict were: A Lich, a Disenchanter, and in the next room a master
mind flayer. JOY.

Managed to lure the mind flayer out and run around him and lock the
door, hoping that he would die to the soldiers in the barracks when I
came back after grabbing the wand. Of course he decides to run off
into the corner so all the soldiers kill each other and not him.
Great. I eventually did kill him without getting my brain sucked by
throwing random weapons at him (remember no Gauntlets of Power yet),
his wand of fire with my "oR and then killing him in the first melee
attack after he was hurt.

Went back to Ludios, wished for (/oW =3D 0:3 thankfully)

3 B?oGenocide - L, ;, R
blessed MM (I had already seen a charging scroll) -> 2 charging
scrolls, another B?oGenocide -> h
speed boots
SDSM (so I could "oLS later)
BG BoH
gauntlets of power

So yeah, rest of this is kinda boring; especially when I got the
second /oW drop in gehennom, which went mostly into Magic Markers.

Other fun stuff:
I gambled on a ?oEA on a +4 HoT, which popped. Replaced it with HoB.
Both Mjollnir and my saber were at +6, tried the Engrave 1 letter
trick to get my saber to +7... +6 again. Tried again but then read the
scroll with the wrong weapon wielded... got lucky that Mjollnir didn't
pop! Whewwwwwwwwwwwwwww. Then made another ?oEW and got to +7 on both,
yay.
At some point dumping my boatloads of gold in the valley I got naked
AC 0. (XL 17 I think)
Managed to get every ring I could want (conflict regen slow digestion
poly control levitation free action) polypiling and in drops. Swapped
em around as needed, decided on free action and regen for the Astral
Plane.
Decided to burn a potion of gain level so I wouldn't have to waste
time in Moloch's Sanctum, ended up getting to 30 anyway with drops
from rodney.
Only got 2 levels and 40 hitpoints from 3 C?oG (two W and a @). I
probably didn't read the W ones in the right places (one was in Ludios
and the other in Sokoban. @ scroll also in sokoban. Read later about
wielding and unwielding but I didn't have enough scrolls despite
wishing for a total of 4 MM (I never got another genocide or charging
drop). Maybe I shoulda wished for the PYEC, eh, got an easy conduct
this way.
As I was running through gehennom I saw a c, stopped, killed it,
grabbed the corpse and Rodney showed up only a couple steps later.
"Here, you take this. And gimme that potion of gain level."
Apparently you don't have to be a wizard to write scrolls on the fly.
I have no idea how lucky I was, but I did have maxed luck and an Int
of 19 and XL in the 20s when I tried to write a gold detection scroll
which I thought I had only erased my previous ones, when in fact I had
never seen one. But I tried it, and it said "a scroll labeled KIRJE".
Huh?? I'm a... Valkyrie, right? I wasn't gonna look a gift horse in
the mouth though.
Managed to make it through the whole plane of air with a blessed
potion of levitation only WHILE confused. Didn't wanna use the ring
slot (free action, conflict), so I had an extra confusion source when
I made it to the astral plane. Fun times.

That's about it. Plus in Gehennom I spent a bunch of time lighting and
digging out the stairs, which was annyoing since I had no MM scrolls
or spellbook. With the HoB my failure rates weren't too bad when I
took the GoP off; I had Light and Identify at only 30% fail by the
end. Anyway 335 HP, regeneration, all 3 types of magic resistances,
dual wielding Mjollnir and a silver saber, AC -40 & invisible makes
the planes kind of a joke.  My pet died and I didn't even bother to
put conflict on. I two-hit both Pestilence and Famine, without either
ever hitting me, saved Death's altar for last but it turned out to be
the second one I tried.

Still a little surprised my score's not in the 4 million range, I
brought all the artifacts I had (Mjollnir, Vorpal, Cleaver,
Dragonbane, all the Sanctum items) with me and lots of gems. Anyone
know why only 3.2 million?

Anyway, gonna try a harder class now, I'm thinking rogue. Woohoo, and
thanks for making it this far RGRN!


